KZ2 patch 6059 (ENHANCEMENT, on by default since an earlier change, LD_TILE_POOL=0 turns it off): the 8x8 main-memory A8R8G8B8 tiles get
their own pool outside the hashed texture cache, keyed by address with an exact byte compare, and their uploads are
batched per submit into the copy list that runs before the draws.

An earlier change (the RE notes): in Corinth Sands' heavy view 99.6 % of the texture cache's new entries are one shape,
8x8 A8R8G8B8 pitch-linear, 256 bytes, in main memory (io offsets 0x63680..0x11D3180), ~400-500 binds a frame,
rewritten between binds (70 % of new entries re-add an evicted key; kept, they need in-place refreshes). Each bind
paid a key lookup, a content hash, a decode, an upload-ring copy with a barrier pair recorded between the draws, an
SRV write, and pushed a real texture out of the 8,192-entry LRU. No cache size removes that (an earlier change's A/B).
- libs/video/rsx_tile_pool.h (new, pure): slots keyed by io offset (open addressing, backward-shift delete), exact
  256-byte compare (hit = no copy), ring order reuse; a slot that a draw of the current chunk reads is never
  rewritten in that chunk (a changed tile gets another slot; FULL when every slot is read by the chunk). Host test
  tools/runtime/test_tile_pool.sh.
- rsx_live_draw.c: texture_srv_slot sends a bind of exactly that shape (location 1, A8R8G8B8 | LINEAR, 8x8, pitch
  0/32, 2D, not cube) to ld_tile_bind; a copy is staged in the upload ring (8 rows at a 256-byte pitch) and recorded
  at the next submit by ld_tile_record into the pool's own copy list, executed just before the chunk's draw list
  (ld_tile_submit at both submit sites; LD_TILE_ALLOCS 8 allocators, each reset after its submit's fence): one
  ResourceBarrier call to COPY_DEST, the copies, one call back. Each slot is a fixed 8x8 R8G8B8A8 texture made
  once, with its own SRV in the CPU heap (SRV_TILE_BASE, LD_TILE_SLOTS_MAX 16,384) holding the guest's A,R,G,B bytes
  with the remap in the component mapping (patch 2046's ld_argb_raw_mapping).
- On by default (checked by hand play on a real display at the Corinth River bridge, lighting right);
  LD_TILE_POOL=0 off; LD_TILE_SLOTS=N (64..16384, default 4096). [tex-tile] every 256 frames
  with RSX_PERF (binds, hits, copies, descriptors, FULL submits, batches, ms in the bind).

