+/* KZ2 patch 6059: the 8x8 main-memory A8R8G8B8 tiles (Killzone 2's per-object ring, ~400-500 binds in a heavy
+ * frame, rewritten between binds) bypass the texture cache. A bind compares the tile's 256 bytes with the pool slot
+ * of its address (rsx_tile_pool.h: keyed by address, exact compare, no hash); a changed or new tile is staged in the
+ * upload ring, and every copy staged in a chunk is recorded at its submit into the pool's own copy list, executed
+ * just before the chunk's draw list: one barrier call into COPY_DEST, the copies, one barrier call back. The draw
+ * list itself gets no copy or barrier for them, the cache keeps its slots for real textures. Each slot is a fixed
+ * 8x8 R8G8B8A8 texture with its own SRV (the guest's A,R,G,B bytes, remap in the component mapping, as patch 2046's
+ * direct upload). On by default; LD_TILE_POOL=0 turns it off; LD_TILE_SLOTS (default 4096) sizes it.
+ * The copy list cycles through LD_TILE_ALLOCS allocators, each reset only after the fence of the submit that used
+ * it has passed. [tex-tile] every 256 frames with RSX_PERF. */
